+# Audit 0.21.0: History filters and the expected window
+
+Method: design review only (detector not applicable, native platform): impeccable critique and
+graphic-design-fundamentals §13 (information design: one message per chart), on
+`day_today_expected_light`, `history_light`.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals §13
+
+| # | Check | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Find one kind fast; see "on time" at a glance. ✅ |
+| 2 | Concept | Filter the list, never the picture; the expected window is a hint, not data. ✅ |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Real sleeps over the faint window. ✅ |
+| 4 | Contrast | The band is deliberately faint (35%) and always named in the legend; it carries no meaning alone. ✅ |
+| 5 | Alignment | Chips on the page gutter. ✅ |
+| 6 | Spacing | Tokens. ✅ |
+| 7 | Typography | Existing roles. ✅ |
+| 8 | Colour | The nap colour, faint, beside its word. ✅ |
+| 9 | Consistency | The same filter chips (blush when picked). ✅ |
+| 10 | Simplicity | One row of chips; the band only today, only while awake. ✅ |
+| 11 | Real size | Phone width. ✅ |
+| 12 | Accessibility | The window is spoken with its times; chips are radio buttons. ✅ |
+| 13 | Production | No new tokens (a documented alpha on an existing data colour). ✅ |
+
+## impeccable critique
+
+| # | Heuristic | Score | Note |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | System status | 4 | The window is where the parent looks. |
+| 2 | Real world | 4 | "Expected next sleep". |
+| 3 | Control | 4 | All is one tap away. |
+| 4 | Consistency | 4 | Same chips everywhere. |
+| 5 | Error prevention | n/a | |
+| 6 | Recognition | 4 | Kinds with entries only. |
+| 7 | Efficiency | 4 | One tap to filter. |
+| 8 | Aesthetic | 4 | Quiet band. |
+| 9 | Error recovery | n/a | |
+| 10 | Help | 3 | Legend explains the band. |
+| | **Total** | **31/32** | |
